name:Benedictio ramorum: Omnípotens sempitérne Redémptor;
office-part:Oratio;
occasion:Dominica in Ramis Palmarum (Missale O.P. 1939, pp. 137-138);
book:set to the Dominican tone of the Orations at the Hours, Processionarium O.P. (1913), pp. 407-408 (pdf = printed + 16); text from the Missale O.P. (1939), pp. 137-138;
commentary:Missale p. 137: "Prior ... ramos arborum ... benedicat eo modo, quo dicuntur Orationes ad Horas." Proc. p. 20: "benedicat eo tono, quo dicuntur Orationes ad Horas", Proc. pp. 20-21 print this prayer pointed for the tone (the flexa sign where the Missal has a semicolon, and at voluísti ‡ where it has a full stop), ending "per ómnia sǽcula sæculórum ‡. ℟. Amen.";
transcriber:generated by tools/hw39/gen_quad6.js with OPMassTones (js/mtones.js), Holy Week task W-B2, 2026-11-27;
